[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444259838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#issuecomment-3444259838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111767","id":3444259838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NSzv-","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T17:52:42Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T17:52:42Z","body":"Got this simplified, albeit in the other direction. That is: instead of directly excluding `_LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES` under certain circumstances or trying to include it granularly, I'll just apply it universally. This meant that even more thirdparty code had to be given patches, but it only affected libraries that *already* recieved patches, so this isn't introducing any \"new\" friction. The one exception is Jolt, but that's simply integrating an [upstream change](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1779), so it too isn't adding any new friction","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444259838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444431548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#issuecomment-3444431548","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111767","id":3444431548,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NTdq8","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T18:42:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T18:42:37Z","body":"Only partially. That's what the `disable_warnings()` function was doing before. However, anything calling thirdparty headers, espcially *in headers*, could still need patches. Otherwise we're having the same problem of system headers potentially using transitive includes","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444431548/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444867849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#issuecomment-3444867849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111767","id":3444867849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NVIMJ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T20:49:28Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T20:49:56Z","body":"> Only partially. That's what the disable_warnings() function was doing before. However, anything calling thirdparty headers, espcially in headers, could still need patches. Otherwise we're having the same problem of system headers potentially using transitive includes\r\n\r\nMakes sense. \r\nThen I got a new idea: How about we create our own wrapper headers that fix the header includes for them? Something like this:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n// \"thirdparty/jolt/wrapper.h\r\n\r\n// _LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES fixes\r\n#include <type_traits>\r\n\r\n#include \"‎thirdparty/jolt_physics/Jolt/Core/Core.h‎\"\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe'd include this file instead of `Jolt/Core/Core.h`, and could disable the `_LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES` for the Jolt library (removing the need for the patches).\r\n\r\nSorry about being so picky about this. But I'm thinking, this is 'just' a build performance PR after all. I'd feel a lot more comfortable if we could find a way to introduce the macro without increasing our maintenance cost / risk of future build failures with these libraries. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3444867849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445087691","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#issuecomment-3445087691","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111767","id":3445087691,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NV93L","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T22:16:43Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T22:16:43Z","body":"If Jolt in particular is a hangup, we could always hold out for an upstream sync where the change is already in place. Otherwise it'd mean editing a lot of files for a wrapper that'd be redundant not too long after\r\n\r\nMore likely you're just wanting to cover your bases about not causing potential breakage. To that end, I just added a new SCons flag: `limit_transitive_includes`. It's enabled by default, but disabling it will exclude the define","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445087691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445112678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#issuecomment-3445112678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111767","id":3445112678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NWD9m","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T22:31:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T22:32:31Z","body":"> More likely you're just wanting to cover your bases about not causing potential breakage. To that end, I just added a new SCons flag: limit_transitive_includes. It's enabled by default, but disabling it will exclude the define\r\n\r\nYes, I mainly wouldn't want this optimization to cause problems or maintenance effort down the line.\r\nThe option to disable this is a great idea. But it won't help people who run into build problems because they won't be able to connect the build problem to the build option on their own. The only _really_ safe option I'd see is _disabling_ it by default, though that would mean nearly nobody would benefit from it...\r\n\r\nThe Jolt example above was just serving as an example to explain a possible alternative to the patches. \r\nMaybe I'm too hesitant to add in patches? I don't know our policy for them. If it's something we're normally happy to take for this kind of improvement I have no further complaints.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3445112678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]